    grouped: each color forms one contiguous run (no interleaving)
    run_length: 1-3 per color; runs sum to H-1 (=W-1)
    corner: equals the last color of both row and col label sequences
  transform:
    rule: for each interior cell (r,c), if row_labels[r] == col_labels[c] then fill with that color, else keep background
    borders: right edge and bottom edge are unchanged

generation_strategy:
  approach: direct construction (input is simple; output is deterministic)
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size N (use 10 or vary in 7-12 for diversity).
    2. Pick K=4-5 distinct non-bg colors.
    3. Partition N-1 into K positive-integer run lengths (each 1-3).
    4. Assign colors to runs in a fixed random order to create row_labels sequence.
    5. Create col_labels using the same color order but independently sampled run lengths (same K-way partition of N-1, each 1-3).
    6. Set corner = last color in the shared ordering.
    7. Fill interior with background; place row_labels on right edge, col_labels on bottom edge, corner at bottom-right.
